//- 4:00 THE LINE OF PURPLES. The yes path starts here, and it's the answer to the cliffhanger: purple is a color your brain invents.

//- The vote slide's Yes link lands here (#/good).
section#good.over-media(data-background-image="img/parthenon.jpg" data-timing="10")
  h2 Democracy works.
  aside.notes
    ul
      li The room voted yes. Democracy works. For now.

//- The purple beat, on three steps: the line, the bend, the fill. The three captions share one spot and swap. pug/partials/_horseshoe.pug draws it, js/purple-beat.js bends it.
section.statement.purple-beat(data-timing="45")
  h2.fragment.fade-out(data-fragment-index="1") Light is a line.
  h2.fragment.fade-in-then-out(data-fragment-index="1") Your brain bends it into a horseshoe.
  h2.fragment.fade-in(data-fragment-index="2") Then fills the gap with purple.
  +purpleBeat
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Light is a line. Every wavelength you can see, in order, violet at one end and red at the other. Past violet is ultraviolet, past red is infrared, and you can't see either.
      li Click: your brain bends the line into a horseshoe, so violet and red end up near each other.
      li Click: then it fills the gap with purple. Purple is your brain mixing the two ends of the line. No single wavelength looks like anything on that bar.
      li The bar has an official name: the line of purples.
      li If challenged: this is the idea of the CIE 1931 chromaticity diagram, tidied into a horseshoe. The real one is lopsided.

//- The cliffhanger's lavender again, as an img in the slide with the same crop, so the eyedropper lines up. Pixel (1524, 1068) of img/lavender.jpg is #6f5895, hue 263, and at the bottom-anchored cover crop (scale 0.5, 267 rows hidden) it lands at 59.5cqw, 55.6cqh.
section.over-media.full-bleed(data-timing="15")
  img(src="img/lavender.jpg" alt="A lavender field in bloom" style="object-position: center bottom;")
  +eyedropper(59.5, 55.6, "#6f5895", "no wavelength")(class="fragment" data-fragment-index="1")
  h2 Your brain made that up.
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Back to the lavender. Click: the eyedropper. It has a hex. It doesn't have a wavelength.
      li Purple is your brain mixing the two ends of the line. No light anywhere is purple on its own.
      li Evidence, and the end of the cliffhanger.
